{"title":"2025 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/c/a9c7cc583137cd786583f9df893ce7124f6b20e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$784$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/eba897e566e3ee4d824ed7b97a8da4f067192884.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 7 \\times 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"167\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/806f78ac25fac6764e4a45c54418042fd74fefea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{4} \\times 7^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/c/a9c7cc583137cd786583f9df893ce7124f6b20e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$784$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is a perfect square because it can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d04eb147f71c362cfeb901c10db5569d84c8f46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2^{2} \\times 7) \\times (2^{2} \\times 7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"148\" height=\"21\" />. The prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/8/8b89cfd0abdb5c9baec504a05f71501c8c45e70d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{2} \\times 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is not a perfect square. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/00386b7bac2de10decaaaeea05ddbe2601b1326f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45 \\times 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> is a perfect square since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33fa04c27e489573c63f46637e0619e4418accf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45 \\times 5 = 3^{2} \\times 5^{2} = (3 \\times 5) \\times (3 \\times 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"286\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What are all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/f/bcf76820e88c2fdb0963923aea81ae74eb378015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j \\leq 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/0/6c09b4ecdd4f930b303705f9df44cae1721ad1d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{3} \\times 3^{2} \\times j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" /> is a perfect square?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because all of the exponents in the prime factorization of a perfect square must be even and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/2/642dea81077b775f66619c0b093d5e3ac52c9df7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{3}$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> has an odd power, we realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/e/51eec2fdce0d4737713acabe21c23c951a32c451.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{x}$\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" /> multiplied by some number, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is an odd integer.\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3e7f7f7537494ac1190cfe8ce31fe5964add90e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/0/51049796b957c6cfb03c81b794affffd895f8cc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j = 2^{3} = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/e/bfe0d48d16847f794a4596b3e802b625fec650ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j = 2 \\times 3^{2} = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"20\" />. All other possible numbers are greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and therefore don't satisfy the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/f/bcf76820e88c2fdb0963923aea81ae74eb378015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j \\leq 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> condition. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/0/940c4d971ae38514b68219cc174a9c1859858e7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 5^{2}$\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> would be the smallest number that introduces another prime factor because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the smallest prime number greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/2/1f237af80b9cdd3c503673764abb9e69a1cdec02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 5^{2} = 50 &gt; 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/d/e1ddd643ebd59e0477b840a1a52abc3671bd63f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 3^{4} &gt; 2^{5} = 32 &gt; 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"175\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the possible numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017224645\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 106/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 617/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5414/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   20.322      1 2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3\n100.00%   20.322      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35151:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017224645 and revision id 281256. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}